With $h^k_j =  rac{2\pi}{N_k}|z^{k\prime}(s^k_j)|$, one has $(D^T)_{ij} = h_i\,\partial_{
u_z}G(z_i-z_j)$ but $(D_s)_{ij} = h_j\,\partial_{
u_z}G(z_i-z_j)$ (the kernels themselves agree via $\partial_{
u_\xi}G(z_j-z_i)=\partial_{
u_z}G(z_i-z_j)$), so $D_s = D^T$ holds only when all arc-length weights are equal (e.g. constant-speed circular components); it fails for the oscillating holes of Example~6. The exact discrete adjoint with respect to the weighted inner product is $D_s = H^{-1}D^TH$ with $H=\mathrm{diag}(h^k_j)$.
